usage: run-feedback-recovery.py [-h] --output OUTPUT --variant {native,mpc}
                                [--terrain {slope,flat}] [--drift-s DRIFT_S]
                                [--recovery-s RECOVERY_S]
                                [--native-hold-s NATIVE_HOLD_S]
                                [--refinement-steps REFINEMENT_STEPS]
                                [--native-rollout-seed]

Fixed-input drift followed by unchanged feedback recovery in Gazebo. The first
.4s reproduces the nearby-pose I31 hold fixture. The native observer runs as a
shadow throughout; feedback starts without resetting state or the observer.
Constant goal XY is retained from the beginning of the run.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT
  --variant {native,mpc}
  --terrain {slope,flat}
  --drift-s DRIFT_S
  --recovery-s RECOVERY_S
  --native-hold-s NATIVE_HOLD_S
  --refinement-steps REFINEMENT_STEPS
  --native-rollout-seed
